pqfreebsd is a post-quantum trusted FreeBSD suite: mac_lomac(4) composition,
an Integrity Evidence ledger, repaired discretionary policy, successive
policy audit, and a gated Forth boot splash. It is not Kyber in the kernel.

This port stages rc.d services, manuals, skills, and loader Forth. It does
not kldload, does not set enabled=1, and does not copy splash art into /boot
until the operator attests (T12).

Intended operation is by a sufficiently advanced large language model that
can operate the skills (interview, test*/one*, Known issues, T14/T16 bounds).
The port cannot prove a model is advanced. OPTION LLM (default) requires
pqfreebsd_llm_attested=YES before oneenforce when installed via this package.
A box installed by hand from the skill tree is a different conjunct.

WWW: https://github.com/brianreborn/pqfreebsd
